From 45c7dbb905d1eca7847ea45a73b5bed9cc73edbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Bryan <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:48:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] fix(plugin-mcp): review fixes for research v2.2

From a second review of commits 8 to 11:

- Version check: an update or delete by id without a usable version
  (ifUpdatedAt "", {}, or a map that does not name the id) was let through
  when the current document could not be read (no read access, a failing
  hook). It is now refused whether or not that read succeeds.
- Collections without timestamps: ifUpdatedAt is neither required nor
  checked, by id or in bulk (it used to refuse a sent version as "gone" by id
  and to refuse unnamed matches in bulk).
- Row ids: the stored document is read with fallbackLocale "none", so rows
  shown from a fallback locale (and their ids) are never adopted. Only array
  and blocks fields of the collection config have rows; a json field holding
  a list of objects is left as sent. An id sent anywhere in the data is
  never filled in for another row, nested rows included.
- Unknown-argument suggestions: no suggestion for names of one or two
  letters, an edit distance of 1 for three or four, and never all or
  overrideLock.
- "nothing to write" mentions the data argument only where it exists. The
  ifUpdatedAt description says that in a collection with drafts the latest
  version is the latest draft.

Tests: 4 more (33 in all), each failing before this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
